// 被拆开”的篡改备份。
func shiftDirectReserve(delta time.Duration) func(*requestBackupV1, *policyBackupV1, *sessionBackupV1) {
	return func(r *requestBackupV1, _ *policyBackupV1, _ *sessionBackupV1) {
		r.ReservedAt = timeJSON(time.Time(r.ReservedAt).Add(delta))
		if d := time.Duration(r.ReserveDuration); d > 0 {
			r.ReserveDeadline = timeJSON(time.Time(r.ReservedAt).Add(d))
		}
		if !time.Time(r.ReserveExpiredAt).IsZero() {
			r.ReserveExpiredAt = r.ReserveDeadline
		}
	}
}
```

Wait, for settled state, settledAt = created+30min. If delta = +5min, settledAt still after reservedAt. OK. If delta = -5min... settledAt still fine. The origin check fires before settlement check anyway? Order in validateRequestTimingAndState: first switch calls validateReservedOrigin (which will contain the new check), then second switch does state-specific. So origin check fires first. Good.

But careful: for delta negative with created = t0 (policy start), reservedAt = t0 - 5min — no check on reservedAt vs policy window exists, so only our new check fires. Good. But to be safe use created = t0 + time.Hour in tests.

